{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.MagnusHookExteriorPower","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.MagnusHookExteriorPower","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.prod_one_add_mul_eq_sum_esymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.prod_one_add_mul_eq_sum_esymm","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusHookExteriorPower.lean#L55-L71","doc":"**All-orders generating function (degree-graded form).**\n`∏ᵢ (1 + t·μᵢ) = Σ_{j=0}^{|ι|} tʲ · e_j(μ)`. The right side is the elementary-symmetric tower;\nits `j`-th term is the reduced-Burau `Λʲ` trace, i.e. (up to the numerically-verified `q`-twist)\nthe hook-`(n−j,1ʲ)` character of the Magnus decay. General `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.esymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.esymm","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusHookExteriorPower.lean#L51-L53","doc":"The `j`-th elementary symmetric sum of `μ`: `e_j = Σ_{|S|=j} ∏_{i∈S} μᵢ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.prod_one_add_mul_eq_sum_powerset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.prod_one_add_mul_eq_sum_powerset","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/MagnusHookExteriorPower.lean#L37-L49","doc":"**All-orders generating function (subset form).** `∏ᵢ (1 + t·μᵢ) = Σ_S t^{|S|} ∏_{i∈S} μᵢ`,\nthe sum over all subsets `S`. This packages every exterior-power degree `j = |S|` into one\nidentity: the coefficient of `t^j` is the `j`-th elementary symmetric sum of `μ`, which the\nprobe identifies (up to the `q`-twist) with the hook-`(n−j,1ʲ)` character of the reduced\nBurau. General `CommRing`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}